/target
/vendor
/swift/.build
# Unanchored on purpose. This read `/web/node_modules` and therefore did not cover
# `chrome/`, so 997 files and 69 MB of chrome's dependency tree were committed and nobody
# noticed - a path-anchored ignore only ever protects the directories somebody remembered.
node_modules/
# The panel document is a build product (scripts/build-web.sh), like the Rust archives.
/web/dist
/chrome/dist
# Tauri's generated capability schemas - derived from capabilities/ at build time.
/crates/mind2t/gen

# Local agent and harness configuration. The real files live outside the repository and are
# symlinked in, so tooling that reads them from the working directory still works while
# nothing about one particular machine's setup ships to anybody who clones. Ignoring is the
# load-bearing half: git stores a symlink AS a symlink, so without these lines a clone would
# receive a pointer into a directory it does not have.
/CLAUDE.md
/.tests-required

# Launch copy. Local working material, not something a public repository should carry.
/docs/launch

# Editor and OS droppings. A vim swap file was committed once and carried the machine's
# account name and hostname in its header, which is not something a public repository
# should be publishing on the author's behalf.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# Platform icon sets `cargo tauri icon` generates for targets this project does not ship.
# It writes Android mipmaps, an iOS AppIcon set and the Windows Store logos whether you want
# them or not; macOS needs `icon.icns` and the four PNGs, Linux needs the PNGs. Ignored rather
# than deleted, because the generator recreates them on every run and a repo about to go public
# should not carry fifty images for platforms it has never built for.
crates/mind2t/icons/android/
crates/mind2t/icons/ios/
crates/mind2t/icons/Square*.png
crates/mind2t/icons/StoreLogo.png
crates/mind2t/icons/icon.ico

# Plans of record. Untracked on purpose: working strategy documents that quote
# the operator directly and name product direction. They are not documentation of
# the product, and they stay on disk.
docs/plans/
